  "stdout": "     1\t/-\n     2\t  ESSubfamilyExtended.lean \u2014 R245 generalized sub-family theorem + staged extensions (R253 admission criterion, R261 A\u2080-constancy, R265 repaired split/layered).\n     3\t\n     4\t  Paper: papers/subfamily-ladder-ceiling-October-11-2026/\n     5\t  Status: [PROVED] \u2014 generalized_subfamily_identity. [PROVED*] (staged, machine-checked, review-cleared) \u2014 admission_criterion, a0_constancy, u_eq_Aqe_div_f, excess_prime_dvd_u, M_const, split_layered_restated, split_layered_repaired\n     6\t  Verification: Lean 4.34.1 + Mathlib v4.34.1 (pinned d13f23b); R262: exit 0 both sides, zero sorrys, axioms standard-only.\n     7\t-/\n     8\t\n     9\t/-\n    10\t  ESSubfamilyExtended.lean \u2014 Lean formalization of R245's generalized\n    11\t  sub-family theorem (Erd\u0151s\u2013Straus parametric families, the r \u2224 XSTEP\u2032/q\n    12\t  regime).\n    13\t\n    14\t  Source: ~/workspace/math-unsolved/ROUND245_DOSSIER.md (Round 245, 2026-10-10).\n    15\t  Rule-9 hostile review: ~/workspace/math-unsolved/review-r245-esext/\n    16\t  (Codex gpt-6-astra / ultra) \u2014 SURVIVES under positive-integer parameter\n    17\t  conventions, with two statement fixes applied here:\n    18\t    (i)  positivity of A and r is now an explicit hypothesis (the reviewer\n    19\t         exhibited a signed-parameter counterexample with C(0) = 0 when\n    20\t         r < 0 is allowed);\n    21\t    (ii) the \"clean dichotomy\" wording is not formalized (only the theorem).\n    22\t  The R253 admission-criterion fold-in is DONE (R266, 2026-10-10): R253's\n    23\t  rule-9 review returned SURVIVES (conditional on R245's integer setup,\n    24\t  which this file supplies via hur/hf), formalized below as\n    25\t  `admission_criterion` (+ `adm_congruence_solvable`). R261's constancy\n    26\t  theorems are folded in below as well (rule-9 review: SURVIVES with the\n    27\t  stronger formula A\u2080(m) = A/gcd(A,qe)); R261's unconditional \u27fa corollary\n    28\t  is NOT formalized as stated (rule-9: false as written) \u2014 only its\n    29\t  corrected restatement `split_layered_restated`.\n    30\t\n    31\t  What is checked: for parameters satisfying R245's hypotheses (with the\n    32\t  positivity fix), every s \u2265 1 in the shifted residue class\n    33\t  s \u2261 \u2212m + 4qeV\u2080 (mod 4qeA\u2080) admits the explicit branch-1 identity\n    34\t  4/(M\u2032t+s) = 1/x + 1/(n\u00b7A\u00b7C) + 1/(B\u00b7C) for all t \u2265 0, with the closed forms\n    35\t  from the dossier. The identity is proved directly (a slick relation chain),\n    36\t  independent of R72's TFAE.\n    37\t\n    38\t  Lean 4.34.1 / Mathlib (pin d13f23b723b8a846827a245b89c10fc7d3f11612).\n    39\t  Zero sorrys. Standard axioms only.\n    40\t-/\n    41\t\n    42\timport Mathlib\n    43\t\n    44\tnamespace ESSubfamilyExtended\n    45\t\n    46\t/-- R245 generalized sub-family theorem, with the rule-9 positivity fix\n    47\t    (A, r > 0 explicit). -/\n    48\ttheorem generalized_subfamily_identity\n    49\t    (q A r e f u m k V\u2080 s : \u2124)\n    50\t    (S Mp : \u2124)\n    51\t    (hq : 0 < q) (hA : 0 < A) (hr : 0 < r) (he : 0 < e)\n    52\t    (hfpos : 0 < f) (hm3 : 3 \u2264 m) (hmod4 : m \u2261 3 [ZMOD 4])\n    53\t    (hS : S = 510510 * q) (hM : Mp = 4 * S)\n    54\t    (hAS : A \u2223 S)\n    55\t    (hur : u * r = A * S)\n    56\t    (hf : f * S = r * q * e)\n    57\t    (hk : m * k = 1 + 4 * u)\n    58\t    (hV\u2080 : q * e * k * V\u2080 \u2261 u [ZMOD A])\n    59\t    (hs : s \u2261 -m + 4 * q * e * V\u2080 [ZMOD 4 * q * e * (A / ((Int.gcd A (q*e*k) : \u2115) : \u2124))])\n    60\t    (h1s : 1 \u2264 s) :\n    61\t    \u2200 t : \u2124, 0 \u2264 t \u2192\n    62\t      (4 : \u211a) / ((Mp * t + s : \u2124) : \u211a) =\n    63\t        1 / ((S * t + q * e * ((s + m) / (4 * q * e)) : \u2124) : \u211a) +\n    64\t        1 / (((Mp * t + s : \u2124) : \u211a) * A *\n    65\t          (((S / A) * k * t + (s * k + 1) / (4 * A) : \u2124) : \u211a)) +\n    66\t        1 / (((r * t + f * ((s + m) / (4 * q * e)) : \u2124) : \u211a) *\n    67\t          (((S / A) * k * t + (s * k + 1) / (4 * A) : \u2124) : \u211a)) := by\n    68\t  -- Basic positivity facts\n    69\t  have hSpos : 0 < S := by rw [hS]; positivity\n    70\t  have hMpos : 0 < Mp := by rw [hM]; positivity\n    71\t  have h4qe : (0:\u2124) < 4 * q * e := by positivity\n    72\t  have h4qene : (4:\u2124) * q * e \u2260 0 := ne_of_gt h4qe\n    73\t  have hAne : (A:\u2124) \u2260 0 := ne_of_gt hA\n    74\t  have h4Ane : (4:\u2124) * A \u2260 0 := by positivity\n    75\t  have hSne : (S:\u2124) \u2260 0 := ne_of_gt hSpos\n    76\t  -- u > 0 from u * r = A * S\n    77\t  have pos_of_mul_pos {a b : \u2124} (h : 0 < a * b) (hb : 0 \u2264 b) : 0 < a := by\n    78\t    by_contra hcon\n    79\t    have hle : a \u2264 0 := le_of_not_gt hcon\n    80\t    have h2 : a * b \u2264 0 := mul_nonpos_of_nonpos_of_nonneg hle hb\n    81\t    omega\n    82\t  have hu : 0 < u := by\n    83\t    have h1 : (0:\u2124) < u * r := by rw [hur]; positivity\n    84\t    exact pos_of_mul_pos h1 hr.le\n    85\t  -- k > 0 from m * k = 1 + 4u\n    86\t  have hkpos : 0 < k := by\n    87\t    have h1 : (0:\u2124) < m * k := by rw [hk]; nlinarith [hu]\n    88\t    rw [mul_comm] at h1\n    89\t    exact pos_of_mul_pos h1 (by omega)\n    90\t  -- The gcd setup: g = gcd(A, qek), A\u2080 = A / g\n    91\t  set g : \u2115 := Int.gcd A (q * e * k) with hgdef\n    92\t  set A\u2080 : \u2124 := A / ((g : \u2115) : \u2124) with hA\u2080def\n    93\t  have hgA : ((g : \u2115) : \u2124) \u2223 A := Int.gcd_dvd_left A (q * e * k)\n    94\t  have hgq : ((g : \u2115) : \u2124) \u2223 q * e * k := Int.gcd_dvd_right A (q * e * k)\n    95\t  have hgpos : 0 < g := by\n    96\t    by_contra hcon\n    97\t    have hle : g \u2264 0 := le_of_not_gt hcon\n    98\t    have h0 : g = 0 := by omega\n    99\t    have hA0 := hgA\n   100\t    rw [h0] at hA0\n   101\t    simp at hA0\n   102\t    omega\n   103\t  have hg1 : (1:\u2124) \u2264 ((g : \u2115) : \u2124) := by exact_mod_cast hgpos\n   104\t  have hAeq : A = A\u2080 * ((g : \u2115) : \u2124) := by\n   105\t    rw [hA\u2080def]\n   106\t    exact (Int.ediv_mul_cancel hgA).symm\n   107\t  have hA\u2080pos : 0 < A\u2080 := by\n   108\t    have h1 : (0:\u2124) < A\u2080 * ((g : \u2115) : \u2124) := by rw [\u2190 hAeq]; exact hA\n   109\t    exact pos_of_mul_pos h1 (by exact_mod_cast Nat.zero_le g)\n   110\t  -- V from 4qe \u2223 s + m (via the residue class)\n   111\t  have hs_dvd : (4:\u2124) * q * e * A\u2080 \u2223 ((-m + 4 * q * e * V\u2080) - s) :=\n   112\t    (Int.modEq_iff_dvd).mp hs\n   113\t  obtain \u27e8V, hV\u27e9 : (4:\u2124) * q * e \u2223 (s + m) := by\n   114\t    have h1 : (4:\u2124) * q * e \u2223 (4 * q * e * A\u2080) := dvd_mul_right _ _\n   115\t    have h2 : (4:\u2124) * q * e \u2223 ((-m + 4 * q * e * V\u2080) - s) := dvd_trans h1 hs_dvd\n   116\t    have h3 : (4:\u2124) * q * e \u2223 (4 * q * e * V\u2080) := dvd_mul_right _ _\n   117\t    have h4 : (4:\u2124) * q * e \u2223 (((-m + 4 * q * e * V\u2080) - s) - 4 * q * e * V\u2080) :=\n   118\t      dvd_sub h2 h3\n   119\t    have heq : (((-m + 4 * q * e * V\u2080) - s) - 4 * q * e * V\u2080) = -(s + m) := by ring\n   120\t    rwa [heq, dvd_neg] at h4\n   121\t  -- hV : s + m = 4 * q * e * V\n   122\t  have hVge : 4 * q * e \u2264 s + m := Int.le_of_dvd (by omega) \u27e8V, hV\u27e9\n   123\t  have hV1 : 1 \u2264 V := by\n   124\t    have h2 : (4:\u2124) * q * e * 1 \u2264 4 * q * e * V := by\n   125\t      rw [mul_one]\n   126\t      rwa [hV] at hVge\n   127\t    exact Int.le_of_mul_le_mul_left h2 h4qe\n   128\t  -- V \u2261 V\u2080 (mod A\u2080): cancel 4qe from 4qeA\u2080 \u2223 4qe(V\u2212V\u2080)\n   129\t  have hsm : s - (-m + 4 * q * e * V\u2080) = 4 * q * e * (V - V\u2080) := by\n   130\t    linear_combination hV\n   131\t  have hs2 : (4:\u2124) * q * e * A\u2080 \u2223 4 * q * e * (V - V\u2080) := by\n   132\t    have h1 : (4:\u2124) * q * e * A\u2080 \u2223 -(((-m + 4 * q * e * V\u2080) - s)) :=\n   133\t      dvd_neg.mpr hs_dvd\n   134\t    have heq : -(((-m + 4 * q * e * V\u2080) - s)) = 4 * q * e * (V - V\u2080) := by\n   135\t      linear_combination hV\n   136\t    rwa [heq] at h1\n   137\t  have hVV\u2080 : A\u2080 \u2223 (V - V\u2080) := by\n   138\t    have h4 : (4:\u2124) * q * e * A\u2080 = (4 * q * e) * A\u2080 := by ring\n   139\t    rw [h4] at hs2\n   140\t    exact (mul_dvd_mul_iff_left h4qene).mp hs2\n   141\t  -- A \u2223 (qek\u00b7V\u2080 \u2212 u) from the solvability congruence\n   142\t  have hAdvd : A \u2223 (q * e * k * V\u2080 - u) := by\n   143\t    have h1 : A \u2223 (u - q * e * k * V\u2080) := (Int.modEq_iff_dvd).mp hV\u2080\n   144\t    have h2 : A \u2223 -(u - q * e * k * V\u2080) := dvd_neg.mpr h1\n   145\t    rwa [neg_sub] at h2\n   146\t  -- A \u2223 qek\u00b7A\u2080 since A = A\u2080\u00b7g and g \u2223 qek\n   147\t  have hAqekA\u2080 : A \u2223 q * e * k * A\u2080 := by\n   148\t    obtain \u27e8l, hl\u27e9 := hgq\n   149\t    exact \u27e8l, by rw [hAeq, hl]; ring\u27e9\n   150\t  -- The c2 core: A \u2223 (qek\u00b7V \u2212 u)\n   151\t  have hcong : A \u2223 (q * e * k * V - u) := by\n   152\t    obtain \u27e8j, hj\u27e9 := hVV\u2080\n   153\t    have e1 : q * e * k * V - u = q * e * k * (A\u2080 * j) + (q * e * k * V\u2080 - u) := by\n   154\t      rw [\u2190 hj]; ring\n   155\t    rw [e1]\n   156\t    apply dvd_add\n   157\t    \u00b7 have e2 : q * e * k * (A\u2080 * j) = (q * e * k * A\u2080) * j := by ring\n   158\t      rw [e2]\n   159\t      exact dvd_mul_of_dvd_left hAqekA\u2080 j\n   160\t    \u00b7 exact hAdvd\n   161\t  -- sk+1 = 4(qeVk \u2212 u)\n   162\t  have hsk : s * k + 1 = 4 * (q * e * V * k - u) := by\n   163\t    have hsV : s = 4 * q * e * V - m := by linear_combination hV\n   164\t    rw [hsV]; linear_combination -hk\n   165\t  -- 4A \u2223 sk+1\n   166\t  have h4Advd : (4:\u2124) * A \u2223 (s * k + 1) := by\n   167\t    rw [hsk]\n   168\t    have h1 : A \u2223 (q * e * V * k - u) := by\n   169\t      have e : q * e * V * k - u = q * e * k * V - u := by ring\n   170\t      rw [e]; exact hcong\n   171\t    exact mul_dvd_mul_left 4 h1\n   172\t  obtain \u27e8Q, hQ\u27e9 := h4Advd\n   173\t  obtain \u27e8P', hP'\u27e9 := hAS\n   174\t  have hP'pos : 0 < P' := by\n   175\t    have h1 : (0:\u2124) < A * P' := by rw [\u2190 hP']; exact hSpos\n   176\t    rw [mul_comm] at h1\n   177\t    exact pos_of_mul_pos h1 hA.le\n   178\t  have hQpos : 0 < Q := by\n   179\t    have h1 : (0:\u2124) < 4 * A * Q := by\n   180\t      rw [\u2190 hQ]\n   181\t      have h2 : 0 < s * k := mul_pos (by omega) hkpos\n   182\t      omega\n   183\t    rw [mul_comm] at h1\n   184\t    exact pos_of_mul_pos h1 (by positivity)\n   185\t  -- Casts to \u211a\n   186\t  have hfQ : (f:\u211a) * S = r * q * e := by exact_mod_cast hf\n   187\t  have hurQ : (u:\u211a) * r = A * S := by exact_mod_cast hur\n   188\t  have hkQ : (m:\u211a) * k = 1 + 4 * u := by exact_mod_cast hk\n   189\t  have hVQ : (s:\u211a) + m = 4 * q * e * V := by exact_mod_cast hV\n   190\t  have hMQ : (Mp:\u211a) = 4 * S := by exact_mod_cast hM\n   191\t  have hPQ : (S:\u211a) = A * P' := by exact_mod_cast hP'\n   192\t  have hQQ : (4:\u211a) * A * Q = s * k + 1 := by exact_mod_cast hQ.symm\n   193\t  -- The per-t identity\n   194\t  intro t ht\n   195\t  have eV : (s + m) / (4 * q * e) = V :=\n   196\t    Int.ediv_eq_of_eq_mul_left h4qene (hV.trans (mul_comm _ _))\n   197\t  have eP : S / A = P' := Int.ediv_eq_of_eq_mul_left hAne (hP'.trans (mul_comm _ _))\n   198\t  have eQ : (s * k + 1) / (4 * A) = Q :=\n   199\t    Int.ediv_eq_of_eq_mul_left h4Ane (hQ.trans (mul_comm _ _))\n   200\t  -- Positivity of the four denominators / witnesses\n   201\t  have hVpos : (0:\u2124) < V := by omega\n   202\t  have hnpos : (0:\u2124) < Mp * t + s := by\n   203\t    have h1 : (0:\u2124) \u2264 Mp * t := mul_nonneg (le_of_lt hMpos) ht\n   204\t    omega\n   205\t  have hxpos : (0:\u2124) < S * t + q * e * V := by\n   206\t    have h1 : (0:\u2124) \u2264 S * t := mul_nonneg (le_of_lt hSpos) ht\n   207\t    have h2 : (0:\u2124) < q * e * V := mul_pos (mul_pos hq he) hVpos\n   208\t    omega\n   209\t  have hBpos : (0:\u2124) < r * t + f * V := by\n   210\t    have h1 : (0:\u2124) \u2264 r * t := mul_nonneg (le_of_lt hr) ht\n   211\t    have h2 : (0:\u2124) < f * V := mul_pos hfpos hVpos\n   212\t    omega\n   213\t  have hCpos : (0:\u2124) < P' * k * t + Q := by\n   214\t    have h1 : (0:\u2124) \u2264 P' * k * t := by\n   215\t      have h2 : (0:\u2124) \u2264 P' * k := mul_nonneg (le_of_lt hP'pos) (le_of_lt hkpos)\n   216\t      exact mul_nonneg h2 ht\n   217\t    omega\n   218\t  have hn : (0:\u211a) < ((Mp * t + s : \u2124) : \u211a) := by exact_mod_cast hnpos\n   219\t  have hx : (0:\u211a) < ((S * t + q * e * V : \u2124) : \u211a) := by exact_mod_cast hxpos\n   220\t  have hB : (0:\u211a) < ((r * t + f * V : \u2124) : \u211a) := by exact_mod_cast hBpos\n   221\t  have hC : (0:\u211a) < ((P' * k * t + Q : \u2124) : \u211a) := by exact_mod_cast hCpos\n   222\t  have hAQ : (0:\u211a) < A := by exact_mod_cast hA\n   223\t  have hSq : (0:\u211a) < S := by exact_mod_cast hSpos\n   224\t  -- Rewrite the goal's edivs to the clean witnesses, then name the \u211a terms\n   225\t  -- (set must precede any push_cast, which would destroy the patterns)\n   226\t  rw [eV, eP, eQ]\n   227\t  set nq : \u211a := ((Mp * t + s : \u2124) : \u211a) with hnqdef\n   228\t  set xq : \u211a := ((S * t + q * e * V : \u2124) : \u211a) with hxqdef\n   229\t  set Bq : \u211a := ((r * t + f * V : \u2124) : \u211a) with hBqdef\n   230\t  set Cq : \u211a := ((P' * k * t + Q : \u2124) : \u211a) with hCqdef\n   231\t  -- The relation chain\n   232\t  have ha : (4:\u211a) * xq = nq + m := by\n   233\t    rw [hxqdef, hnqdef]; push_cast\n   234\t    linear_combination (-t) * hMQ - hVQ\n   235\t  have hb : Bq * S = r * xq := by\n   236\t    rw [hBqdef, hxqdef]; push_cast\n   237\t    linear_combination (V : \u211a) * hfQ\n   238\t  have hc : (4:\u211a) * A * Cq = k * nq + 1 := by\n   239\t    rw [hCqdef, hnqdef]; push_cast\n   240\t    linear_combination (-4 * k * t) * hPQ + hQQ + (-k * t) * hMQ\n   241\t  have hmac : m * (A * Cq) = xq + u * nq := by\n   242\t    linear_combination (m / 4) * hc + (nq / 4) * hkQ - (1 / 4) * ha\n   243\t  have keyS : (A * xq - u * Bq) * S = 0 := by\n   244\t    linear_combination (-u) * hb + (-xq) * hurQ\n   245\t  have key : A * xq = u * Bq := by\n   246\t    have h0 : A * xq - u * Bq = 0 := by\n   247\t      rcases mul_eq_zero.mp keyS with h | h\n   248\t      \u00b7 exact h\n   249\t      \u00b7 exact absurd h (ne_of_gt hSq)\n   250\t    exact sub_eq_zero.mp h0\n   251\t  have hBCne : Bq * Cq \u2260 0 := mul_ne_zero hB.ne' hC.ne'\n   252\t  have hNACXne : nq * A * Cq * xq \u2260 0 :=\n   253\t    mul_ne_zero (mul_ne_zero (mul_ne_zero hn.ne' hAQ.ne') hC.ne') hx.ne'\n   254\t  have hNACne : nq * A * Cq \u2260 0 :=\n   255\t    mul_ne_zero (mul_ne_zero hn.ne' hAQ.ne') hC.ne'\n   256\t  have e1 : (1:\u211a) / (Bq * Cq) = (u * nq) / (nq * A * Cq * xq) := by\n   257\t    rw [div_eq_div_iff hBCne hNACXne]\n   258\t    have e : nq * A * Cq * xq = (u * nq) * (Bq * Cq) := by\n   259\t      linear_combination (nq * Cq) * key\n   260\t    rw [e, one_mul]\n   261\t  have e2 : (1:\u211a) / (nq * A * Cq) = xq / (nq * A * Cq * xq) := by\n   262\t    rw [div_eq_div_iff hNACne hNACXne]; ring\n   263\t  have esum : (1:\u211a) / (nq * A * Cq) + 1 / (Bq * Cq) =\n   264\t      (xq + u * nq) / (nq * A * Cq * xq) := by\n   265\t    rw [e2, e1, \u2190 add_div]\n   266\t  have hACne : (A:\u211a) * Cq \u2260 0 := mul_ne_zero hAQ.ne' hC.ne'\n   267\t  have em : (xq + u * nq) / (nq * A * Cq * xq) = m / (nq * xq) := by\n   268\t    have hnx : nq * A * Cq * xq = (nq * xq) * (A * Cq) := by ac_rfl\n   269\t    rw [hnx, \u2190 hmac]\n   270\t    exact mul_div_mul_right _ _ hACne\n   271\t  have hfin : (m:\u211a) / (nq * xq) = 4 / nq - 1 / xq := by\n   272\t    have ha' : (m:\u211a) = 4 * xq - nq := by linarith [ha]\n   273\t    have h1 : nq \u2260 0 := hn.ne'\n   274\t    have h2 : xq \u2260 0 := hx.ne'\n   275\t    rw [ha']\n   276\t    field_simp\n   277\t  have hmain : (1:\u211a) / (nq * A * Cq) + 1 / (Bq * Cq) = m / (nq * xq) := by\n   278\t    rw [esum, em]\n   279\t  have key2 : (1:\u211a) / (nq * A * Cq) + 1 / (Bq * Cq) + 1 / xq = 4 / nq := by\n   280\t    linarith [hmain, hfin]\n   281\t  calc (4:\u211a) / nq = 1 / (nq * A * Cq) + 1 / (Bq * Cq) + 1 / xq := key2.symm\n   282\t    _ = 1 / xq + 1 / (nq * A * Cq) + 1 / (Bq * Cq) := by ring\n   283\t\n   284\tend ESSubfamilyExtended\n   285\t\n   286\tnamespace ESSubfamilyExtended\n   287\t\n   288\t/-! ## R253: sharpened admission criterion (rule-9 review: SURVIVES, R266)\n   289\t\n   290\tReview: ~/workspace/math-unsolved/review-r253-admission/review-transcript.txt\n   291\t(Codex gpt-6-astra / ultra). Verdict: \"The criterion survives, conditional on\n   292\tR245 supplying the asserted integer setup. I found no counterexample.\"\n   293\tThe integrality condition (f \u2223 A\u00b7qe, i.e. u = Aqe/f \u2208 \u2124) is now an explicit\n   294\thypothesis; the R245 setup in this file supplies it via `hur`/`hf`. The\n   295\t28,561-valuation-tuple exhaustive check is cited, not re-proved.\n   296\t-/\n   297\t\n   298\t/-- R253 per-prime five-case criterion, as a standalone Prop over the\n   299\t    valuations \u03b1 = v_p(A), \u03b2 = v_p(qe), \u03c6 = v_p(f), \u03ba = v_p(k). Case (e)\n   300\t    (\"no condition\") contributes nothing. -/\n   301\tdef AdmCond (\u03b1 \u03b2 \u03c6 \u03ba : \u2115) : Prop :=\n   302\t  (\u03b2 \u2265 \u03b1 \u2192 \u03c6 \u2264 \u03b2) \u2227 \u00ac(\u03b2 < \u03b1 \u2227 \u03c6 > \u03b1) \u2227\n   303\t  (\u03b2 < \u03b1 \u2192 \u03c6 = \u03b1 \u2192 \u03ba = 0) \u2227\n   304\t  (\u03b2 < \u03b1 \u2192 \u03b2 < \u03c6 \u2192 \u03c6 < \u03b1 \u2192 \u03ba \u2264 \u03b1 - \u03c6)\n   305\t\n   306\t/-- The local valuation inequality is equivalent to the five-case\n   307\t    criterion (R253's (*), direction-audited; `omega` closes it). -/\n   308\ttheorem adm_val_criterion_iff (\u03b1 \u03b2 \u03c6 \u03ba : \u2115) (h\u03c6 : \u03c6 \u2264 \u03b1 + \u03b2) :\n   309\t    min \u03b1 (\u03b2 + \u03ba) \u2264 \u03b1 + \u03b2 - \u03c6 \u2194 AdmCond \u03b1 \u03b2 \u03c6 \u03ba := by\n   310\t  unfold AdmCond\n   311\t  omega\n   312\t\n   313\t/-- Solvability of the admission congruence (qek)V \u2261 u (mod A) is\n   314\t    equivalent to gcd(A, qek) \u2223 u (Bezout form of R253's \"Solvability \u27fa\n   315\t    d \u2223 u\"). -/\n   316\ttheorem adm_congruence_solvable (A qe k u : \u2115) (hA : 0 < A) :\n   317\t    (\u2203 V : \u2124, ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) * V \u2261 (u : \u2124) [ZMOD (A : \u2124)]) \u2194\n   318\t      ((Nat.gcd A (qe * k) : \u2115) : \u2124) \u2223 (u : \u2124) := by\n   319\t  have hcast : Int.gcd (A : \u2124) ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) = ((Nat.gcd A (qe * k) : \u2115) : \u2124) := by\n   320\t    rw [Int.gcd_natCast_natCast]\n   321\t  constructor\n   322\t  \u00b7 rintro \u27e8V, hV\u27e9\n   323\t    rw [Int.modEq_iff_dvd] at hV\n   324\t    have hdA : ((Nat.gcd A (qe * k) : \u2115) : \u2124) \u2223 (A : \u2124) := by\n   325\t      exact_mod_cast Nat.gcd_dvd_left A (qe * k)\n   326\t    have hdq : ((Nat.gcd A (qe * k) : \u2115) : \u2124) \u2223 ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) := by\n   327\t      exact_mod_cast Nat.gcd_dvd_right A (qe * k)\n   328\t    have h1 : ((Nat.gcd A (qe * k) : \u2115) : \u2124) \u2223 ((u : \u2124) - ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) * V) :=\n   329\t      dvd_trans hdA hV\n   330\t    have h2 : ((Nat.gcd A (qe * k) : \u2115) : \u2124) \u2223 ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) * V :=\n   331\t      dvd_mul_of_dvd_left hdq V\n   332\t    have h3 := dvd_add h1 h2\n   333\t    have heq : ((u : \u2124) - ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) * V) + ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) * V = (u : \u2124) := by\n   334\t      ring\n   335\t    rwa [heq] at h3\n   336\t  \u00b7 rintro \u27e8c, hc\u27e9\n   337\t    have hbez : ((Nat.gcd A (qe * k) : \u2115) : \u2124)\n   338\t        = (A : \u2124) * Int.gcdA (A : \u2124) ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124)\n   339\t          + ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) * Int.gcdB (A : \u2124) ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) := by\n   340\t      rw [\u2190 hcast, Int.gcd_eq_gcd_ab]\n   341\t    refine \u27e8Int.gcdB (A : \u2124) ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) * c, ?_\u27e9\n   342\t    rw [Int.modEq_iff_dvd]\n   343\t    have key : (u : \u2124) - ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) * (Int.gcdB (A : \u2124) ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) * c)\n   344\t        = (A : \u2124) * (Int.gcdA (A : \u2124) ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) * c) := by\n   345\t      rw [hc, hbez]; ring\n   346\t    exact \u27e8Int.gcdA (A : \u2124) ((qe * k : \u2115) : \u2124) * c, key\u27e9\n   347\t\n   348\t/-- R253 sharpened admission criterion: with u = A\u00b7qe/f \u2208 \u2115 (the\n   349\t    integrality the rule-9 review made a hypothesis), gcd(A, qe\u00b7k) \u2223 u\n   350\t    iff the five-case per-prime criterion holds at every prime. -/\n   351\ttheorem admission_criterion (A qe f k : \u2115)\n   352\t    (hA : 0 < A) (hqe : 0 < qe) (hf : 0 < f) (hk : 0 < k)\n   353\t    (hfint : f \u2223 A * qe) :\n   354\t    Nat.gcd A (qe * k) \u2223 (A * qe / f) \u2194\n   355\t      \u2200 p : \u2115, p.Prime \u2192\n   356\t        AdmCond (A.factorization p) (qe.factorization p)\n   357\t          (f.factorization p) (k.factorization p) := by\n   358\t  have hAne : A \u2260 0 := ne_of_gt hA\n   359\t  have hqene : qe \u2260 0 := ne_of_gt hqe\n   360\t  have hkne : k \u2260 0 := ne_of_gt hk\n   361\t  have hfne : f \u2260 0 := ne_of_gt hf\n   362\t  have hqkne : qe * k \u2260 0 := mul_ne_zero hqene hkne\n   363\t  have hAqe : A * qe \u2260 0 := mul_ne_zero hAne hqene\n   364\t  have hgpos : 0 < Nat.gcd A (qe * k) :=\n   365\t    Nat.pos_of_dvd_of_pos (Nat.gcd_dvd_left A (qe * k)) hA\n   366\t  have hune : A * qe / f \u2260 0 := by\n   367\t    have h1 : A * qe / f * f = A * qe := Nat.div_mul_cancel hfint\n   368\t    rintro h0\n   369\t    rw [h0, zero_mul] at h1\n   370\t    have h2 : 0 < A * qe := by positivity\n   371\t    omega\n   372\t  have h\u03c6 : \u2200 p : \u2115, p.Prime \u2192\n   373\t      f.factorization p \u2264 A.factorization p + qe.factorization p := by\n   374\t    intro p _\n   375\t    have hle0 := (Nat.factorization_le_iff_dvd hfne hAqe).mpr hfint\n   376\t    have hlep := (Finsupp.le_def.mp hle0) p\n   377\t    have hmul := Nat.factorization_mul hAne hqene\n   378\t    have h2p := DFunLike.congr_fun hmul p\n   379\t    rw [Finsupp.add_apply] at h2p\n   380\t    omega\n   381\t  have hfac : \u2200 p : \u2115, p.Prime \u2192\n   382\t      (Nat.gcd A (qe * k)).factorization p\n   383\t        = min (A.factorization p) (qe.factorization p + k.factorization p) \u2227\n   384\t      (A * qe / f).factorization p\n   385\t        = A.factorization p + qe.factorization p - f.factorization p := by\n   386\t    intro p hp\n   387\t    have h1 : (Nat.gcd A (qe * k)).factorization p\n   388\t        = min (A.factorization p) ((qe * k).factorization p) := by\n   389\t      have h := DFunLike.congr_fun (Nat.factorization_gcd hAne hqkne) p\n   390\t      rw [Finsupp.inf_apply] at h\n   391\t      exact h\n   392\t    have hmul := Nat.factorization_mul hqene hkne\n   393\t    have h2p := DFunLike.congr_fun hmul p\n   394\t    rw [Finsupp.add_apply] at h2p\n   395\t    have hdiv := Nat.factorization_div hfint\n   396\t    have hmul2 := Nat.factorization_mul hAne hqene\n   397\t    have h3p := DFunLike.congr_fun hdiv p\n   398\t    rw [Finsupp.tsub_apply] at h3p\n   399\t    have h4p := DFunLike.congr_fun hmul2 p\n   400\t    rw [Finsupp.add_apply] at h4p\n   401\t    constructor <;> omega\n   402\t  rw [\u2190 Nat.factorization_le_iff_dvd hgpos.ne' hune]\n   403\t  constructor\n   404\t  \u00b7 intro h p hp\n   405\t    have hle := (Finsupp.le_def.mp h) p\n   406\t    obtain \u27e8h1, h3\u27e9 := hfac p hp\n   407\t    rw [h1, h3] at hle\n   408\t    exact (adm_val_criterion_iff _ _ _ _ (h\u03c6 p hp)).mp hle\n   409\t  \u00b7 intro h\n   410\t    rw [Finsupp.le_def]\n   411\t    intro p\n   412\t    by_cases hpp : p.Prime\n   413\t    \u00b7 obtain \u27e8h1, h3\u27e9 := hfac p hpp\n   414\t      rw [h1, h3]\n   415\t      exact (adm_val_criterion_iff _ _ _ _ (h\u03c6 p hpp)).mpr (h p hpp)\n   416\t    \u00b7 have z1 : (Nat.gcd A (qe * k)).factorization p = 0 :=\n   417\t        (Nat.factorization_eq_zero_iff _ _).mpr (Or.inl hpp)\n   418\t      have z2 : (A * qe / f).factorization p = 0 :=\n   419\t        (Nat.factorization_eq_zero_iff _ _).mpr (Or.inl hpp)\n   420\t      omega\n   421\t\n   422\t/-! ## R261: A\u2080-constancy (rule-9 review: SURVIVES with stronger formula, R266)\n   423\t\n   424\tReview: ~/workspace/math-unsolved/review-r261-a0constancy/review-transcript.txt\n   425\t(Codex gpt-6-astra / ultra). Verdict: \"The A\u2080-constancy theorem survives.\n   426\tThe appended corollary does not: both '\u27fa' statements are false as written.\"\n   427\tThe valuation argument proves the stronger explicit formula\n   428\tA\u2080(m) = A/gcd(A, qe), formalized here. The unconditional \u27fa corollary is\n   429\tNOT formalized as stated; its corrected restatement (reviewer's repair:\n   430\tequivalences hold when at least one parent set is nonempty) is\n   431\t`split_layered_restated` below.\n   432\t-/\n   433\t\n   434\t/-- R261 (S1): u = A\u00b7qe/f as an exact equation, avoiding division. -/\n   435\ttheorem u_eq_Aqe_div_f (A qe f u : \u2115) (hf : 0 < f) (hu_eq : u * f = A * qe) :\n   436\t    u = A * qe / f := by\n   437\t  have h1 : u * f / f = u := Nat.mul_div_cancel u hf\n   438\t  rw [\u2190 h1, hu_eq]\n   439\t\n   440\t/-- R261 (S3): an excess prime (v_p(f) < v_p(A)) divides u = A\u00b7qe/f. -/\n   441\ttheorem excess_prime_dvd_u (A qe f : \u2115) (hA : 0 < A) (hqe : 0 < qe) (hf : 0 < f)\n   442\t    (hfint : f \u2223 A * qe) (p : \u2115) (hp : p.Prime)\n   443\t    (hlt : f.factorization p < A.factorization p) :\n   444\t    p \u2223 A * qe / f := by\n   445\t  have hAne : A \u2260 0 := ne_of_gt hA\n   446\t  have hqene : qe \u2260 0 := ne_of_gt hqe\n   447\t  have hfne : f \u2260 0 := ne_of_gt hf\n   448\t  obtain \u27e8c, hc\u27e9 := hfint\n   449\t  have hcne : c \u2260 0 := by\n   450\t    rintro rfl\n   451\t    rw [mul_zero] at hc\n   452\t    have h2 : 0 < A * qe := by positivity\n   453\t    omega\n   454\t  have hdiv : A * qe / f = c := by\n   455\t    rw [hc]; exact Nat.mul_div_cancel_left c hf\n   456\t  rw [hdiv]\n   457\t  have h1 : (f * c).factorization = (A * qe).factorization := by rw [\u2190 hc]\n   458\t  have h1p := DFunLike.congr_fun h1 p\n   459\t  have hmul1 := Nat.factorization_mul hfne hcne\n   460\t  have hmul2 := Nat.factorization_mul hAne hqene\n   461\t  have h2p := DFunLike.congr_fun hmul1 p\n   462\t  have h3p := DFunLike.congr_fun hmul2 p\n   463\t  rw [Finsupp.add_apply] at h2p h3p\n   464\t  rw [h2p, h3p] at h1p\n   465\t  have hpos : 1 \u2264 c.factorization p := by omega\n   466\t  exact dvd_trans (dvd_pow_self p (by omega)) (Nat.ordProj_dvd c p)\n   467\t\n   468\t/-- R261 pinning lemma (cases (d),(e)): at an excess prime with\n   469\t    v_p(f) < v_p(A), p \u2223 u, so p \u2224 D\u2080 = 1+4u, so v_p(k) = 0 for m\u00b7k = D\u2080. -/\n   470\ttheorem pinning_lemma (A qe f : \u2115) (hA : 0 < A) (hqe : 0 < qe) (hf : 0 < f)\n   471\t    (hfint : f \u2223 A * qe) (p : \u2115) (hp : p.Prime)\n   472\t    (hex : qe.factorization p < A.factorization p)\n   473\t    (hlt : f.factorization p < A.factorization p)\n   474\t    (m : \u2115) (hm : m \u2223 1 + 4 * (A * qe / f))\n   475\t    (k : \u2115) (hk : m * k = 1 + 4 * (A * qe / f)) :\n   476\t    k.factorization p = 0 := by\n   477\t  have hpu : p \u2223 A * qe / f :=\n   478\t    excess_prime_dvd_u A qe f hA hqe hf hfint p hp hlt\n   479\t  have hnp : \u00ac p \u2223 1 + 4 * (A * qe / f) := by\n   480\t    intro hdiv\n   481\t    have h4u : p \u2223 4 * (A * qe / f) := dvd_mul_of_dvd_right hpu 4\n   482\t    have h1 : (p : \u2124) \u2223 ((1 + 4 * (A * qe / f) : \u2115) : \u2124) := by exact_mod_cast hdiv\n   483\t    have h2 : (p : \u2124) \u2223 ((4 * (A * qe / f) : \u2115) : \u2124) := by exact_mod_cast h4u\n   484\t    have h3 : (p : \u2124) \u2223 ((1 + 4 * (A * qe / f) : \u2115) : \u2124) - ((4 * (A * qe / f) : \u2115) : \u2124) :=\n   485\t      dvd_sub h1 h2\n   486\t    have heq : ((1 + 4 * (A * qe / f) : \u2115) : \u2124) - ((4 * (A * qe / f) : \u2115) : \u2124) = 1 := by\n   487\t      push_cast; ring\n   488\t    have h4 : (p : \u2124) \u2223 (1 : \u2124) := by rwa [heq] at h3\n   489\t    have h5 : p \u2223 1 := Int.natCast_dvd_natCast.mp h4\n   490\t    have h6 : p \u2264 1 := Nat.le_of_dvd (by norm_num) h5\n   491\t    have h7 : 2 \u2264 p := hp.two_le\n   492\t    omega\n   493\t  by_contra hne\n   494\t  have hpk : p \u2223 k := by\n   495\t    have h1k : 1 \u2264 k.factorization p := Nat.one_le_iff_ne_zero.mpr hne\n   496\t    exact dvd_trans (dvd_pow_self p (by omega)) (Nat.ordProj_dvd k p)\n   497\t  have hpmk : p \u2223 m * k := dvd_mul_of_dvd_right hpk m\n   498\t  rw [hk] at hpmk\n   499\t  exact hnp hpmk\n   500\t\n   501\t/-- R261: the R253 criterion pins \u03ba_p = 0 at every excess prime for an\n   502\t    admitted complementary divisor (case (c) directly; cases (d),(e) via\n   503\t    the pinning lemma; case (b) excludes \u03c6_p > \u03b1_p). -/\n   504\ttheorem admission_pinning (A qe f k : \u2115) (hA : 0 < A) (hqe : 0 < qe) (hf : 0 < f)\n   505\t    (hfint : f \u2223 A * qe)\n   506\t    (hadm : \u2200 p : \u2115, p.Prime \u2192\n   507\t      AdmCond (A.factorization p) (qe.factorization p)\n   508\t        (f.factorization p) (k.factorization p))\n   509\t    (m : \u2115) (hk : m * k = 1 + 4 * (A * qe / f)) :\n   510\t    \u2200 p : \u2115, p.Prime \u2192 qe.factorization p < A.factorization p \u2192\n   511\t      k.factorization p = 0 := by\n   512\t  intro p hp hex\n   513\t  obtain \u27e8_, h2, h3, _\u27e9 := hadm p hp\n   514\t  by_cases h\u03c6 : f.factorization p = A.factorization p\n   515\t  \u00b7 exact h3 hex h\u03c6\n   516\t  \u00b7 have hlt : f.factorization p < A.factorization p := by\n   517\t      have hle : f.factorization p \u2264 A.factorization p := by\n   518\t        by_contra hcon\n   519\t        push_neg at hcon\n   520\t        exact h2 \u27e8hex, hcon\u27e9\n   521\t      omega\n   522\t    exact pinning_lemma A qe f hA hqe hf hfint p hp hex hlt m \u27e8k, hk.symm\u27e9 k hk\n   523\t\n   524\t/-- R261 stronger formula (per the rule-9 review): an admitted k gives\n   525\t    A\u2080 = A/gcd(A, qe\u00b7k) = A/gcd(A, qe), a shape-level constant. -/\n   526\ttheorem a0_constancy_formula (A qe k : \u2115) (hA : 0 < A) (hqe : 0 < qe) (hk : 0 < k)\n   527\t    (hpin : \u2200 p : \u2115, p.Prime \u2192\n   528\t      qe.factorization p < A.factorization p \u2192 k.factorization p = 0) :\n   529\t    A / Nat.gcd A (qe * k) = A / Nat.gcd A qe := by\n   530\t  have hAne : A \u2260 0 := ne_of_gt hA\n   531\t  have hqene : qe \u2260 0 := ne_of_gt hqe\n   532\t  have hkne : k \u2260 0 := ne_of_gt hk\n   533\t  have hg1 : 0 < Nat.gcd A (qe * k) :=\n   534\t    Nat.pos_of_dvd_of_pos (Nat.gcd_dvd_left A (qe * k)) hA\n   535\t  have hg2 : 0 < Nat.gcd A qe :=\n   536\t    Nat.pos_of_dvd_of_pos (Nat.gcd_dvd_left A qe) hA\n   537\t  have hd1 : A / Nat.gcd A (qe * k) \u2260 0 := by\n   538\t    have h := Nat.div_pos (Nat.le_of_dvd hA (Nat.gcd_dvd_left A (qe * k))) hg1\n   539\t    omega\n   540\t  have hd2 : A / Nat.gcd A qe \u2260 0 := by\n   541\t    have h := Nat.div_pos (Nat.le_of_dvd hA (Nat.gcd_dvd_left A qe)) hg2\n   542\t    omega\n   543\t  apply Nat.eq_of_factorization_eq hd1 hd2\n   544\t  intro p\n   545\t  have e1 := Nat.factorization_div (Nat.gcd_dvd_left A (qe * k))\n   546\t  have e2 := Nat.factorization_div (Nat.gcd_dvd_left A qe)\n   547\t  have p1 := DFunLike.congr_fun e1 p\n   548\t  have p2 := DFunLike.congr_fun e2 p\n   549\t  rw [Finsupp.tsub_apply] at p1 p2\n   550\t  by_cases hpp : p.Prime\n   551\t  \u00b7 have g1 : (Nat.gcd A (qe * k)).factorization p\n   552\t        = min (A.factorization p) ((qe * k).factorization p) := by\n   553\t      have h := DFunLike.congr_fun\n   554\t        (Nat.factorization_gcd hAne (mul_ne_zero hqene hkne)) p\n   555\t      rw [Finsupp.inf_apply] at h\n   556\t      exact h\n   557\t    have g2 : (Nat.gcd A qe).factorization p\n   558\t        = min (A.factorization p) (qe.factorization p) := by\n   559\t      have h := DFunLike.congr_fun (Nat.factorization_gcd hAne hqene) p\n   560\t      rw [Finsupp.inf_apply] at h\n   561\t      exact h\n   562\t    have m1 := Nat.factorization_mul hqene hkne\n   563\t    have m1p := DFunLike.congr_fun m1 p\n   564\t    rw [Finsupp.add_apply] at m1p\n   565\t    by_cases hex : qe.factorization p < A.factorization p\n   566\t    \u00b7 have hkz := hpin p hpp hex\n   567\t      rw [p1, p2, g1, g2, m1p, hkz]\n   568\t      omega\n   569\t    \u00b7 push_neg at hex\n   570\t      rw [p1, p2, g1, g2, m1p]\n   571\t      omega\n   572\t  \u00b7 have z1 : (Nat.gcd A (qe * k)).factorization p = 0 :=\n   573\t      (Nat.factorization_eq_zero_iff _ _).mpr (Or.inl hpp)\n   574\t    have z2 : (Nat.gcd A qe).factorization p = 0 :=\n   575\t      (Nat.factorization_eq_zero_iff _ _).mpr (Or.inl hpp)\n   576\t    have zA : A.factorization p = 0 :=\n   577\t      (Nat.factorization_eq_zero_iff _ _).mpr (Or.inl hpp)\n   578\t    rw [p1, p2]\n   579\t    omega\n   580\t\n   581\t/-- R261 A\u2080-constancy: two admitted complementary divisors give the same A\u2080. -/\n   582\ttheorem a0_constancy (A qe k\u2081 k\u2082 : \u2115) (hA : 0 < A) (hqe : 0 < qe)\n   583\t    (hk\u2081 : 0 < k\u2081) (hk\u2082 : 0 < k\u2082)\n   584\t    (hpin\u2081 : \u2200 p : \u2115, p.Prime \u2192\n   585\t      qe.factorization p < A.factorization p \u2192 k\u2081.factorization p = 0)\n   586\t    (hpin\u2082 : \u2200 p : \u2115, p.Prime \u2192\n   587\t      qe.factorization p < A.factorization p \u2192 k\u2082.factorization p = 0) :\n   588\t    A / Nat.gcd A (qe * k\u2081) = A / Nat.gcd A (qe * k\u2082) := by\n   589\t  rw [a0_constancy_formula A qe k\u2081 hA hqe hk\u2081 hpin\u2081,\n   590\t    a0_constancy_formula A qe k\u2082 hA hqe hk\u2082 hpin\u2082]\n   591\t\n   592\t/-- R261 A\u2080-constancy, packaged for admitted m\u2081, m\u2082 (pinning derived from\n   593\t    the R253 criterion via `admission_pinning`). -/\n   594\ttheorem a0_constancy_admitted (A qe f k\u2081 k\u2082 m\u2081 m\u2082 : \u2115)\n   595\t    (hA : 0 < A) (hqe : 0 < qe) (hf : 0 < f)\n   596\t    (hk\u2081 : 0 < k\u2081) (hk\u2082 : 0 < k\u2082) (hfint : f \u2223 A * qe)\n   597\t    (hadm\u2081 : \u2200 p : \u2115, p.Prime \u2192\n   598\t      AdmCond (A.factorization p) (qe.factorization p)\n   599\t        (f.factorization p) (k\u2081.factorization p))\n   600\t    (hadm\u2082 : \u2200 p : \u2115, p.Prime \u2192\n   601\t      AdmCond (A.factorization p) (qe.factorization p)\n   602\t        (f.factorization p) (k\u2082.factorization p))\n   603\t    (hkD\u2081 : m\u2081 * k\u2081 = 1 + 4 * (A * qe / f))\n   604\t    (hkD\u2082 : m\u2082 * k\u2082 = 1 + 4 * (A * qe / f)) :\n   605\t    A / Nat.gcd A (qe * k\u2081) = A / Nat.gcd A (qe * k\u2082) :=\n   606\t  a0_constancy A qe k\u2081 k\u2082 hA hqe hk\u2081 hk\u2082\n   607\t    (admission_pinning A qe f k\u2081 hA hqe hf hfint hadm\u2081 m\u2081 hkD\u2081)\n   608\t    (admission_pinning A qe f k\u2082 hA hqe hf hfint hadm\u2082 m\u2082 hkD\u2082)\n   609\t\n   610\t/-- R261 M-constancy: M(m) = 4\u00b7qe\u00b7A\u2080(m) is shape-level constant. -/\n   611\ttheorem M_const (A qe k\u2081 k\u2082 : \u2115) (hA : 0 < A) (hqe : 0 < qe)\n   612\t    (hk\u2081 : 0 < k\u2081) (hk\u2082 : 0 < k\u2082)\n   613\t    (hpin\u2081 : \u2200 p : \u2115, p.Prime \u2192\n   614\t      qe.factorization p < A.factorization p \u2192 k\u2081.factorization p = 0)\n   615\t    (hpin\u2082 : \u2200 p : \u2115, p.Prime \u2192\n   616\t      qe.factorization p < A.factorization p \u2192 k\u2082.factorization p = 0) :\n   617\t    4 * qe * (A / Nat.gcd A (qe * k\u2081)) = 4 * qe * (A / Nat.gcd A (qe * k\u2082)) := by\n   618\t  rw [a0_constancy A qe k\u2081 k\u2082 hA hqe hk\u2081 hk\u2082 hpin\u2081 hpin\u2082]\n   619\t\n   620\t/-! ## R261 corrected corollary restatement (rule-9 reviewer's repair, R266)\n   621\t\n   622\tThe unconditional \u27fa as stated in R261 is FALSE (reviewer counterexample:\n   623\tq=29, A=10, r=510510 \u2014 three admitted values with EMPTY parent sets, which\n   624\tare both identical and disjoint). The reviewer's prescribed repair:\n   625\t\"retain R256's valid domain and replace both \u27fa symbols by \u21d2; alternatively,\n   626\twithin that domain, the equivalences hold if at least one of the two parent\n   627\tsets is nonempty.\" Formalized here is the alternative: with parent-set\n   628\tdetermination (R256's valid domain) as a hypothesis and at least one parent\n   629\tset nonempty, both \u27fa statements hold. The determination itself is NOT\n   630\tproved here (R256's review is MIXED \u2014 see ROUND266_DOSSIER.md).\n   631\t-/\n   632\t\n   633\t/-- R261 split/layered dichotomy, corrected restatement: parent sets\n   634\t    determined by the residue class mod g (R256's valid domain, cited);\n   635\t    with at least one parent set nonempty, identical \u27fa equal residues and\n   636\t    disjoint \u27fa distinct residues. -/\n   637\ttheorem split_layered_restated (Parents : Finset \u2115) (g res\u2081 res\u2082 : \u2115)\n   638\t    (P\u2081 P\u2082 : Finset \u2115)\n   639\t    (hdet\u2081 : P\u2081 = Parents.filter (fun s' => s' % g = res\u2081 % g))\n   640\t    (hdet\u2082 : P\u2082 = Parents.filter (fun s' => s' % g = res\u2082 % g))\n   641\t    (hne : P\u2081.Nonempty) :\n   642\t    (P\u2081 = P\u2082 \u2194 res\u2081 % g = res\u2082 % g) \u2227\n   643\t      (Disjoint P\u2081 P\u2082 \u2194 res\u2081 % g \u2260 res\u2082 % g) := by\n   644\t  have heq : res\u2081 % g = res\u2082 % g \u2192 P\u2081 = P\u2082 := by\n   645\t    intro h\n   646\t    rw [hdet\u2081, hdet\u2082, h]\n   647\t  refine \u27e8\u27e8?_, heq\u27e9, \u27e8?_, ?_\u27e9\u27e9\n   648\t  \u00b7 intro hP\n   649\t    obtain \u27e8s', hs'\u27e9 := hne\n   650\t    have hs1 : s' \u2208 Parents.filter (fun s' => s' % g = res\u2081 % g) := by\n   651\t      rw [\u2190 hdet\u2081]; exact hs'\n   652\t    have hs2 : s' \u2208 Parents.filter (fun s' => s' % g = res\u2082 % g) := by\n   653\t      rw [\u2190 hdet\u2082, \u2190 hP]; exact hs'\n   654\t    have h1 : s' % g = res\u2081 % g := (Finset.mem_filter.mp hs1).2\n   655\t    have h2 : s' % g = res\u2082 % g := (Finset.mem_filter.mp hs2).2\n   656\t    omega\n   657\t  \u00b7 intro hD hcon\n   658\t    have hD2 : Disjoint P\u2082 P\u2082 := heq hcon \u25b8 hD\n   659\t    have hne2 : P\u2082.Nonempty := heq hcon \u25b8 hne\n   660\t    obtain \u27e8x, hx\u27e9 := hne2\n   661\t    exact (Finset.disjoint_left.mp hD2 hx) hx\n   662\t  \u00b7 intro hne'\n   663\t    rw [Finset.disjoint_left]\n   664\t    intro x hx1 hx2\n   665\t    have hx1' : x \u2208 Parents.filter (fun s' => s' % g = res\u2081 % g) := by\n   666\t      rw [\u2190 hdet\u2081]; exact hx1\n   667\t    have hx2' : x \u2208 Parents.filter (fun s' => s' % g = res\u2082 % g) := by\n   668\t      rw [\u2190 hdet\u2082]; exact hx2\n   669\t    have h1 : x % g = res\u2081 % g := (Finset.mem_filter.mp hx1').2\n   670\t    have h2 : x % g = res\u2082 % g := (Finset.mem_filter.mp hx2').2\n   671\t    exact hne' (by omega)\n   672\t\n   673\tend ESSubfamilyExtended\n   674\t\n   675\tnamespace ESSubfamilyExtended\n   676\t\n   677\t/-- R265 repaired split/layered dichotomy \u2014 fold of the rule-9-reviewed\n   678\t    [PROVED*] theorem (see ROUND265_DOSSIER.md \"Formalizable restatement\").\n   679\t    Rule-9 review (Bunny, Q-10, 2026-10-10): \"SURVIVES under cited\n   680\t    assumptions\", 9/9 checks, \"no Lean claim\" (#agents ts\n   681\t    1791669332.842259, 16:05 PDT confirmation \"conditional SURVIVES\").\n   682\t    (a) SPLIT and (b) LAYERED are forced UNCONDITIONALLY (no nonemptiness\n   683\t    hypothesis \u2014 this is the repair over `split_layered_restated`);\n   684\t    (c) both upgrade to \u27fa under the sharp hypothesis that at least one\n   685\t    parent set is nonempty. The determination is R256's, cited as a\n   686\t    hypothesis, not proved here. -/\n   687\ttheorem split_layered_repaired (Parents : Finset \u2115) (g res\u2081 res\u2082 : \u2115)\n   688\t    (P\u2081 P\u2082 : Finset \u2115)\n   689\t    (hdet\u2081 : P\u2081 = Parents.filter (fun s' => s' % g = res\u2081 % g))\n   690\t    (hdet\u2082 : P\u2082 = Parents.filter (fun s' => s' % g = res\u2082 % g)) :\n   691\t    (res\u2081 % g \u2260 res\u2082 % g \u2192 Disjoint P\u2081 P\u2082) \u2227\n   692\t    (res\u2081 % g = res\u2082 % g \u2192 P\u2081 = P\u2082) \u2227\n   693\t    ((P\u2081 \u222a P\u2082).Nonempty \u2192\n   694\t      (Disjoint P\u2081 P\u2082 \u2194 res\u2081 % g \u2260 res\u2082 % g) \u2227\n   695\t      (P\u2081 = P\u2082 \u2194 res\u2081 % g = res\u2082 % g)) := by\n   696\t  have heq : res\u2081 % g = res\u2082 % g \u2192 P\u2081 = P\u2082 := by\n   697\t    intro h\n   698\t    rw [hdet\u2081, hdet\u2082, h]\n   699\t  have hdis : res\u2081 % g \u2260 res\u2082 % g \u2192 Disjoint P\u2081 P\u2082 := by\n   700\t    intro hne'\n   701\t    rw [Finset.disjoint_left]\n   702\t    intro x hx1 hx2\n   703\t    have hx1' : x \u2208 Parents.filter (fun s' => s' % g = res\u2081 % g) := by\n   704\t      rw [\u2190 hdet\u2081]; exact hx1\n   705\t    have hx2' : x \u2208 Parents.filter (fun s' => s' % g = res\u2082 % g) := by\n   706\t      rw [\u2190 hdet\u2082]; exact hx2\n   707\t    have h1 : x % g = res\u2081 % g := (Finset.mem_filter.mp hx1').2\n   708\t    have h2 : x % g = res\u2082 % g := (Finset.mem_filter.mp hx2').2\n   709\t    exact hne' (by omega)\n   710\t  refine \u27e8hdis, heq, ?_\u27e9\n   711\t  intro hU\n   712\t  obtain \u27e8x, hx\u27e9 := hU\n   713\t  rcases Finset.mem_union.mp hx with hx1 | hx2\n   714\t  \u00b7 obtain \u27e8hP, hD\u27e9 :=\n   715\t      split_layered_restated Parents g res\u2081 res\u2082 P\u2081 P\u2082 hdet\u2081 hdet\u2082 \u27e8x, hx1\u27e9\n   716\t    exact \u27e8hD, hP\u27e9\n   717\t  \u00b7 obtain \u27e8hP, hD\u27e9 :=\n   718\t      split_layered_restated Parents g res\u2082 res\u2081 P\u2082 P\u2081 hdet\u2082 hdet\u2081 \u27e8x, hx2\u27e9\n   719\t    refine \u27e8\u27e8?_, ?_\u27e9, \u27e8?_, ?_\u27e9\u27e9\n   720\t    \u00b7 intro hdp\n   721\t      exact Ne.symm (hD.mp (disjoint_comm.mp hdp))\n   722\t    \u00b7 intro hne'\n   723\t      exact disjoint_comm.mpr (hD.mpr (Ne.symm hne'))\n   724\t    \u00b7 intro hpp\n   725\t      exact (hP.mp hpp.symm).symm\n   726\t    \u00b7 intro hrr\n   727\t      exact (hP.mpr hrr.symm).symm\n   728\t\n   729\tend ESSubfamilyExtended\n.github/workflows/lean_action_ci.yml\nMathproofs/ESIdentity.lean\nMathproofs/ESBarrier.lean\nMathproofs/TransDAG.lean\nMathproofs/AbstractLock.lean\nMathproofs/ESRefinedSieveInverse.lean\nMathproofs/ESQRCoreCount.lean\nMathproofs/CollatzGapSinh.lean\nMathproofs/ESX0S1S3.lean\nMathproofs/ESQadicBoundary.lean\nMathproofs/CompositeSuppression.lean\nMathproofs/Girth5Floor3vRegression.lean\nMathproofs/ESFiberCompatComposite.lean\nMathproofs/ESPrimeSquareT2.lean\nMathproofs/ESDescentCovering.lean\nMathproofs/TranslationMarch.lean\nMathproofs/ESBranchTwo.lean\nMathproofs/Girth5Floor3v.lean\nMathproofs/ESMod7UniversalFamilies.lean\nMathproofs/VoidUnion.lean\nMathproofs/CollatzGapC22C25.lean\nMathproofs/VoidDefectHom.lean\nMathproofs/Girth5Extremal.lean\nMathproofs/WitnessComplexThm13.lean\nMathproofs/ESFiveSevenForcing.lean\nMathproofs/ESSubfamilyExtended.lean\nMathpro