ons remain separate. Descent and\n    84\tq-adic results still require the stated QQ/M23/R74 inputs where used. The\n    85\tbarrier is a CRT escape kernel with supplied local obstructions; the integer\n    86\tpolynomial Schinzel\u2013Mordell implication remains unformalized. Global graph\n    87\textremality now implies the score ceiling through exact edge accounting.\n    88\t\n    89\t## Checking instructions\n    90\t\n    91\tRequires [elan](https://github.com/leanprover/elan) (the Lean toolchain manager)\n    92\tand Lean 4.34.1 + Mathlib v4.34.1 (pinned by `lean-toolchain` and\n    93\t`lake-manifest.json`):\n    94\t\n    95\t```bash\n    96\tlake exe cache get   # fetch precompiled Mathlib oleans (large download)\n    97\tlake build           # builds all of Mathproofs\n    98\t```\n    99\t\n   100\tCI (`.github/workflows/lean_action_ci.yml`) runs the full build on every push.\n   101\t`#print axioms <theorem>` on any entry above reproduces the axiom column;\n   102\tnothing here is claimed on the basis of a `sorry`.\n   103\t\n   104\t## Formalizations in progress (not yet published)\n   105\t\n   106\tThe following local formalizations are still being worked through the\n   107\tpublication pipeline \u2014 they are **not** part of this release:\n   108\t\n   109\t- `ESCubicClassify.lean` (R89, quarantined \u2014 known `Int.Coprime` breakage, not registered)\n   110\t- `DonorKernel.lean`, `ESUBBranchIsolation.lean`\n   111\t  (verification status ambiguous or in flight \u2014 excluded pending confirmation)\n   112\t\n   113\t## SS-004 verification checkpoint (issue #10)\n   114\t\n   115\tThe six staged results `admission_criterion`, `a0_constancy`, `u_eq_Aqe_div_f`,\n   116\t`excess_prime_dvd_u`, `M_const`, and `split_layered_repaired` passed compiled-statement/\n   117\taxiom checks and `leanchecker --verbose Mathproofs.ESSubfamilyExtended` (exit 0) at\n   118\tcommit `c9d3c0ebb6474c5b134b2c85cae36ff84cd2af43`, using Lean 4.34.1 (compiler\n   119\t`504