), and run a full `lake build`. Record the exact outcome on this issue.\n2. **Verify the SS-004 batch.** For each of `admission_criterion`, `a0_constancy`, `u_eq_Aqe_div_f`, `excess_prime_dvd_u`, `M_const`, `split_layered_repaired` in `Mathproofs/ESSubfamilyExtended.lean`: confirm the built artefact contains the theorem with no `sorry` anywhere in its dependency path and record its `#print axioms` report.\n3. **Deliverable — one PR to this repo**, naming and closing this ticket:\n   - For every theorem that kernel-verifies with standard-only axioms: promote its catalogue status to **[PROVED]** in `FORMALIZATION_CATALOGUE.md` (and in `CONTENTS.md` if it mirrors the label), citing the build + axiom evidence in the PR body.\n   - For any theorem that does **not** verify: do not change its label and do not weaken any statement. Name the exact defect in the PR body and in a comment on this issue, and the coordinator will file the follow-up formalization ticket from it.\n   - No other files change. No statement in `ESSubfamilyExtended.lean` is edited under this ticket; if a proof edit turns out to be necessary, stop and report it as the defect instead.\n\n## Gates\n\nIndependent review before merge (you are never your own reviewer); the coordinator merges on PASS. You never merge your own PR. Fated pre-empts: park with an exact resume checkpoint (file, theorem, commit, build state). Report the claim, the build result, and your progress on this issue thread; blockers also go to your role inbox the same cycle.\n\n**What this ticket does NOT show or authorize:** no new theorem is claimed by it; a label promotion under it means \"independently kernel-verified on the assignee's machine at the recorded commit\", nothing more. It does not touch Iggy's math-formalization backlog and does not assign the formalize-everything book queue.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/derekblair/math-proofs/issues/10/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,